Asset licenses and AI attribution
--------------------------------
The MIT grant above applies to executable code, generation scripts and
documentation. Media and authored level data are separately dedicated under
CC0-1.0 as described in LICENSE-ASSETS.md; see CREDITS.md and
sound_sources.json for individual source credits and license notices.

Significant code, procedural asset generators, original models, textures, UI
artwork, sound design and musical compositions were developed with
Codex GPT-6 Astra Medium. Music and most effects are rendered by editable
procedural synthesis scripts; they are not recordings generated by an audio
model. The approved menu title banner was generated with OpenAI image
generation. Human contributions include game direction, review, testing and
authored tutorial/arena designs. These credits describe tools and contributions
and do not claim that an AI system owns copyright.

Retained third-party ChipTone layers: Tom Vian / SFB Games, CC0-1.0.
Historical Kenney and James Gargette (cinameng) contributions remain credited
in CREDITS.md although their recordings have been replaced.
